--------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTICE: Derived-work and methodology acknowledgments
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

solo-agent-kit is a methodology-driven, lightweight personal agent for
one-person companies. Its modules are independent, standard-library
implementations of ideas the author validated in earlier projects. This
project borrows METHODOLOGY (not code) from the following, which are
acknowledged for transparency:

1. OptMem (permanent agent memory, hierarchical summary tree + hybrid
   semantic retrieval) — methodology source for solo/memory.py
   Author: zhengjinjun1975 (local, E:\optmem)

2. codegraph (code impact analysis) — methodology source for solo/code.py
   Author: zhengjinjun1975 (local, E:\optmem\codegraph)

3. zh-writing-checker (six-dimension Chinese writing quality check) —
   methodology source for solo/writing.py
   Author: zhengjinjun1975 — https://github.com/zhengjinjun1975/zh-writing-checker

4. factory-ontology-kit (ontology-driven data QA framework) — methodology
   source for solo/ontology.py
   Author: zhengjinjun1975 — https://github.com/zhengjinjun1975/factory-ontology

5. Buzz (Block, Inc.) — Apache-2.0, https://github.com/block/buzz
   Design ideas absorbed (not code): agent-first JSON CLI with graded exit
   codes, "small enough to hold in your head" auditability, tool-calls-are-
   the-output principle.

6. AHE: Agentic Harness Engineering (arXiv 2604.25850) — design ideas for
   observability-driven harness evolution (not code).

7. MemGPT/Letta, Khoj, Mem0, nanobot — general design inspiration for
   memory layering (not code).

These are METHODOLOGY borrowings (concept/architecture), not source-code
copies. Where any file is substantially derived from a specific project's
code, that file carries its own header noting the source and license.
